# Assemble — core rules

Assemble is an assurance platform for UK public sector digital and capital delivery. Full spec in
`docs/spec/`. Stack adaptations (Prisma, single Next app) in `docs/spec/ADAPTATIONS.md`.

## Locked product decisions — do not relitigate

- **One Next.js App Router app on Vercel.** Do not reintroduce a separate Express org-tool server.
- **Standards are data.** Never hardcode a criterion, a point number, a criterion count, or
  "14 points" in application code once criteria tables exist.
- **AI proposes, humans judge.** No code path may write a judgement without a confirming user id.
  AI services write to suggestion rows only, never directly to judgements, entities, relationships
  or evidence.
- **Scoring lives in `lib/scoring`** as a pure function. Never compute an index, verdict, gap or
  contribution in a component, route handler or PDF layer.
- **Read from delivery tools, never replace them.** Do not build a backlog, sprint board, test
  manager, document store or risk register.

## Vocabulary — one word per concept, in code and in UI

`engagement` · `criterion` · `judgement` · `verdict` (`met` / `at-risk` / `not-met` /
`not-assessed`) · `Preparedness Index` · `evidence` · `gap` · `move` · `chain` · `accountability` ·
`circle` / `role` / `product` · `vacant` · `framework` (for NISTA/ISO/RIBA, as distinct from
`standard`) · `superseded`.

Never use: workspace, project, score (for a single criterion), rating, RAG, pass/fail, issue,
document (for evidence), recommendation, unstaffed, archived.

## Refuse these patterns

- A colour used as the only carrier of meaning. Every verdict needs glyph + label + wash.
- `outline: none` or any removal of focus styling.
- A raw Tailwind palette class (`bg-blue-500`, `text-red-600`). Semantic tokens only.
- Hardcoded hex values in components. Every colour comes from tokens CSS.
- `Date.now()` inside scoring or freshness logic. `now` is injected.
- An index of `0` when data is insufficient. It is `null`, rendered `—`.
- String concatenation to build a user-facing sentence.
- A gap without a remedy attached.
- Machine-translated Welsh reaching an export.

## When uncertain

If a task appears to require breaking one of the rules above, stop and say so rather than working
around it.
